        "original_id": "e5bfbf52-67b6-50dd-9505-b08a0c914983",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Young\n- Events: 1952 Individual Speedway World Championship, London Riders' Championship, South Australian Championship\n- Topics: speedway achievements\n\nFacts:\n- In 1952, Jack Young won the Individual Speedway World Championship with 14 points.\n- In 1952, Jack Young became the first rider to win the Individual Speedway World Championship twice and the first rider to win it in consecutive years.\n- In 1953, Jack Young won the London Riders' Championship.\n- In 1954, Jack Young won the London Riders' Championship again.\n- Between 1948 and 1964, Jack Young won the South Australian Championship nine times.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
