        "text": "Page: 1952 Individual Speedway World Championship. Sentence: Australian rider Jack Young became the first ever dual winner (and the first to win two in a row) when he won his second straight World Championship after scoring 14 points.\nPage: Jack Young (speedway rider). Sentence: He also won the London Riders' Championship 1953 and 1954 and was a nine time South Australian Champion between 1948 and 1964.",
